        "date": "2026-11-13T21:30:25Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(fixtures): a flipped setup's fixtures are judged against the carried stock's shape, not its box\n\nThe carried-workholding clause judged each fixture by its world AABB, so\na vise gripping a carried part's sides, or soft jaws whose nest pocket\nholds it, \"stood inside\" the part and refused the post. The box stays the\nbroad phase; a fixture it flags is now read by its closed world mesh,\ncolumn by column: the Z spans the mesh puts on the column's vertical line\n(new FixtureMesh::steel_on_line) against the carried material, with a\n0.01 mm contact tolerance (centre line and four lines 0.01 mm beside it).\nThe mesh only acquits: open/refused/coarse meshes, unreadable lines, a\nspent visit budget and sub-cell footprints keep the box depth. Columns\nthat cannot deepen the worst depth are skipped, so the scan stays bounded.\n\nFixes #1530\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
