      "message": "fix(fixtures): the carried-stock mesh reading sees steel between the columns and never reads an inconsistent winding as air\n\nM3's review of 279ac89f found two ways the mesh cleared steel the box\nrefuses:\n- Between the columns: only each column's centre line (and four lines\n  0.01 mm beside it) was read, so a 0.19 mm post or lip standing in the\n  part between two lines cleared. Every rectangle spanned by four\n  material columns (trimmed by the contact tolerance) is now read whole\n  against the material the four share (FixtureMesh::steel_in_prism):\n  facets clipped to the rectangle reaching into the slab convict; no\n  facet over it is no steel; otherwise one line decides the slab, which\n  holds no surface. Nothing inside the material is sampled.\n- A line whose winding goes negative or does not close (an inside-out\n  shell over another) reads None, so the box stands.\n\nThe nudge step is capped at 0.1 micron so a line far from the origin is\nnot moved off a feature. Decision record updated with the argument.\n\nRefs #1530\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
