        "date": "2026-11-13T22:59:19Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(fixtures): keep the box where a carried rectangle is too slim to read\n\nSecond M3 review of PR #1549:\n- A rectangle between the carried columns that the contact tolerance\n  inverts (pitch under 0.02 mm) is tested as slim before the\n  off-footprint test, so it keeps the box depth instead of clearing.\n- A facet index the mesh does not hold reads as unread (line and\n  prism), and a non-finite clip reads as steel over the slab: no\n  early-out can clear on degenerate input.\n- Pins: the rectangle read's contact band (0.03 mm refused, 0.005 mm\n  contact) and trim (a 0.015 mm post 0.012 mm off a line, refused at 3),\n  the slim rectangle at a 0.015 mm pitch (refused at 3, as the box), and\n  a setup turned 90 degrees about Z judged in its turned frame.\n- Decision record: \"at most one pitch into\" the material at a side face\n  (filed as #1580), the 0.02 mm contact strip, the re-measured budget.\n\nRefs #1530\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
